  "encoding": {
    "normalization": "each histogram is normalized WITHIN its group: plotted value is the share of that group's rows in the bin, so the 90-row and 852-row groups are comparable; raw counts are kept under groups.*.counts and are never drawn",
    "bin_edges": "shared by both groups, 30 bins of width 0.02 over [0.40, 1.00]",
    "smoothing": "none: no kernel density estimate.  Both distributions are bounded above by cosine 1 and the failures mass against that bound, where a Gaussian kernel would put weight past 1 and round off a shoulder the data does not have; a shared-edge histogram carries the same comparison with no edge artifact",
